**Description:** The Director of Operations is an experienced operations leader who contributes to CoRe’s mission by executing operational strategy and ensuring compliance. This position will oversee internal operations, including human resources, database and grants management, information technology, and office services.

**Department**: The Director of Operations leads the Operations Department, and reports to the Executive Director.

**Terms of Employment:** Fulltime/Exempt

**Location:** Hybrid in Brooklyn

**Special Requirements:** The nature of this position requires frequent in-person attendance at CoRe’s offices and occasional in-person attendance at on-site and off-site events on evenings, weekends, and holidays. This position also requires the ability to lift/move up to 20lbs around the office, such as supplies, furniture, etc.

**Salary Range:** $140,000-$165,000

All CoRe employees are expected to abide by organizational rules and protocols, complete their duties as assigned, and meet relevant organizational and programmatic goals and expectations.

All CoRe managers are expected to foster a culture of excellence and innovation, to invest in the development of their direct reports, and to be exceptional stewards of CoRe’s reputation in the community.

**Key Duties and Responsibilities include the following:**

**1. Execute operational strategy to meet organizational goals, which may include:**

* Draft, review, and revise CoRe policies on various operational matters such as database management, human resources, etc.; ensure compliance with such policies; and promote best practices across CoRe;
* Develop and oversee organizational systems, structures, and tools;
* Ensure ongoing alignment between operational, financial, and programmatic objectives;
* Provide thought-partnership to ED on long-term operational strategy; and
* Promote a management culture rooted in client-centeredness, teamwork, open communication, prudent risk taking, innovation, mentoring, and accountability.

**2. Lead day-to-day operations, which may include:**

* Ensure the effective, efficient, and secure operation of internal processes and systems;
* Take a leadership role in employee and labor relations within CoRe and administer and provide guidance on employee and labor relations policies to leadership team as needed;
* Directly manage Operations Department, including team members handling human resources, payroll, information technology, office services, grants management, and more;
* Partner closely with CoRe’s internal and external teams and vendors to promote strong fiscal, technological, and operational health; and
* Other duties as assigned.

**3. Ensure organizational compliance with legal, regulatory, funder, contractual, and insurance requirements, which may include:**

* Maintain up-to-date knowledge of, and ensure CoRe’s policies and practices are compliant with, insurance requirements and federal, state, and local laws and regulations;
* Review, draft, negotiate, and ensure organizational compliance with contracts;
* Other duties as assigned.

**Qualifications:**

* Applicants must have at least 10 years of relevant experience, including serving in operational leadership or in-house counsel at a complex or government organization;
* JD and admission to the New York State bar strongly preferred;
* Strong organizational skills, exceptional attention to detail, and experience managing multiple assignments and projects simultaneously;
* Excellent analytical, research, and writing skills;
* Familiarity with contract law; labor and employment law; and legal ethics and compliance;
* Ability to create and monitor budgets, including vendor sourcing;
* Ability to collect, analyze and use data to guide program and process improvement;
* Demonstrated commitment to mentorship and supporting the professional development of others;
* Demonstrated experience engaging in creative problem solving, strategic flexibility, and good judgment; and
* Experience working in a unionized environment preferred, with the ability to build positive labor-management relations.

CoRe is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will be afforded equal employment opportunities without discrimination because of race, religion/creed, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, sexual orientation, military status, predisposing genetic characteristics, victim of domestic violence status or marital status.

Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis.

To apply, please email a cover letter and resume, with the subject “Director of Operations,” to Ramina Davidson, Executive Director, at rdavidson@communitiesresist.org.

